            <ArticleTitle>Breast education for schoolgirls; why, what, when, and how?</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/tbj.12945</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Schools are fundamental settings for health education and adolescent females are an important group for promoting positive breast habits. We surveyed 2089 schoolgirls (11-18 years) to provide evidence for, and guidance on, breast education for schoolgirls. 26% reported negative feelings about their breasts and 87% reported ≥ one breast concern. 72% wanted to know more about breast cancer (69% rating this extremely important). &gt;50% wanted to know more about breast sag and breast pain. Preferred delivery format was age eleven (50%), girls only taught sessions (41%) with female teachers (43%). A need for breast education and delivery preferences was identified.</AbstractText>
